  "method": "Matched before/after frame for each ship. Glacier uses the earlier orthographic camera. Delta uses one fitted perspective camera for both versions, including browser comparison. The archived flat-camera renders remain available in the selected folder. Each painting is 1024 square; gallery frames add 64 pixels on all sides. The 3504 × 2336 sheets use a 1440 × 960 tracing grid.",
  "scope_of_counts": "Feature marks and sky tests cover specified points only. Some informed fitting. The historical glazing marks predate these models. The skyline sampler uses a regular grid and three brightness thresholds. It excludes unstable columns, including fine aerials. The camera fit excludes both the dish and mast. The third held-out mark shares a stack with two training collars. The fitted lens is an approximation.",
